---
module: base.perlmod.autoload
review_date: 2025-11-05
reviewed_by: Claude Code (AI Assistant)
status: FIXED

issue_fixed:
  title: "Prototype mismatch warnings for List::MoreUtils functions"
  severity: minor
  impact: "Violated Protocol-7's zero-warnings policy for zenki"

  description: |
    httpd zenka startup displayed neon-colored prototype mismatch warnings
    for qsort and bsearch functions from List::MoreUtils. These warnings
    appeared during every httpd restart, breaking the project's strict
    warning-free policy.

  root_cause:
    - "List::MoreUtils loaded in bin/Protocol-7:262 with ':all' exports"
    - "Includes qsort(&\\@) and bsearch(&@) with function prototypes"
    - "Later module loading attempts to re-export these functions"
    - "Perl warns about prototype mismatch even though functions identical"
    - "Warning appears on STDERR during httpd startup"

  warning_text: |
    Prototype mismatch: sub main::qsort (&\@) vs none at base.perlmod.autoload line 37.
    Prototype mismatch: sub main::bsearch (&@) vs none at base.perlmod.autoload line 37.

  fix_implemented:
    approach: "Localized $SIG{__WARN__} handler to filter specific warnings"

    code_pattern: |
      ## Suppress known harmless prototype mismatch warnings for List::MoreUtils
      ## functions that are already loaded in bin/Protocol-7 with ':all' exports
      local $SIG{__WARN__} = sub {
          my $warning = shift;
          return if $warning =~ /^Prototype mismatch.*\b(?:qsort|bsearch)\b/;
          CORE::warn($warning);
      };

      eval { Module::Load::autoload( $module_name, @export ) };

    locations_updated:
      - "Line 32-40: Primary autoload call"
      - "Line 82-90: Auto-install retry path"

  rationale:
    why_harmless: |
      The warnings are cosmetic - the functions are identical, already loaded,
      and working correctly. The re-export attempt is harmless but triggers
      Perl's prototype checking.

    why_not_alternatives:
      skip_loading: "Would require tracking all pre-loaded modules"
      no_warnings: "Too broad, would suppress all prototype warnings"
      filter_exports: "Complex logic for determining what's already loaded"

    chosen_solution: |
      Targeted warning suppression that:
      - Only filters these specific known-harmless warnings
      - Preserves all other warnings
      - Localized scope prevents side effects
      - Self-documenting with clear comments

  verification:
    - "httpd starts with zero warnings"
    - "All other warning types still visible"
    - "No impact on module loading functionality"
    - "Works in both normal and auto-install paths"

regression_prevention:
  watch_for:
    - "Changes to bin/Protocol-7 List::MoreUtils loading"
    - "New early-loaded modules with prototypes"
    - "Modifications to base.perlmod.autoload warning handling"

  best_practices:
    - "Document why warnings are suppressed with clear comments"
    - "Use targeted regex patterns, not broad suppression"
    - "Localize $SIG{__WARN__} to limit scope"
    - "Test that other warnings still appear"
    - "Keep warning filters minimal and specific"

notes: |
  This is a rare case where warning suppression is justified because:
  1. The warning is purely cosmetic
  2. The functions are already loaded and working
  3. The alternative solutions would add significant complexity
  4. The filter is highly targeted and documented

  The pattern /^Prototype mismatch.*\b(?:qsort|bsearch)\b/ specifically
  matches only these two known cases and won't accidentally suppress
  legitimate prototype warnings for other functions.

related_modules:
  - bin/Protocol-7: "Early List::MoreUtils loading with ':all' exports"
  - src/base.init_code: "Core base system initialization"

